From: TB710FU clean board
Subject: [PATCH] Record every startup callback completion in the live log

Reason: the device now reaches later startup phases, while the verbose startup
line is printed before each callback and cannot distinguish an entry from a
return. A phase-specific marker would require one build per observed boundary.
Record one bounded completion marker for every startup callback instead, so one
diagnostic build covers KMEM, ZALLOC, SYSCTL, EARLY_BOOT and later callbacks.

This is diagnostic-only: callback order, arguments, startup cursor and callback
behavior remain unchanged. The global 250 ms live-log poll throttle remains in
force, and the marker is emitted only when live-log is active.

Verification: applies after patch 0016 to the selected startup.c. Native
arm64e compilation and strict prelink must be rerun before hardware use.

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/startup.c b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -494,13 +494,11 @@ kernel_startup_initialize_upto(startup_subsystem_id_t upto)
 		startup_phase = cur->subsystem - 1;
 		kernel_startup_log(cur->subsystem);
 		cur->func(cur->arg);
 #if defined(XNU_TB710FU_LIVE_LOG) && XNU_TB710FU_LIVE_LOG
-		if (tb710fu_live_log_active() &&
-		    cur->subsystem == STARTUP_SUB_KMEM &&
-		    cur->rank == STARTUP_RANK_FIRST) {
-			kprintf("TB710FU live log: KMEM rank-0 callback returned\n");
+		if (tb710fu_live_log_active()) {
+			kprintf("TB710FU live log: startup callback returned [%u, rank %d] %p\n",
+			    cur->subsystem, cur->rank, cur->arg);
 			tb710fu_live_log_poll();
 		}
 #endif
